<worksheet >
    <title>APP-3 Surface Integrals</title>
  <introduction>
    <p>To earn an M on this outcome, you will need to set up, correctly evaluate and simplify the surface integral. 
      To earn a P on this outcome, you will need to set up the integral and show progress on evaluating it.</p>
  </introduction>  
  <page>
    <exercise workspace="2.5in"><p>Evaluate the surface integral <m>\iint_S f(x,y,z)\,dS</m>, 
      where <m>f(x,y,z) = yz</m> and <m>S</m> is the part of the cylinder <m>x^2 + y^2 = 4</m> 
      that lies between the planes <m>z = 0</m> and <m>z = 3</m> in the first octant.</p></exercise>
  </page>
</worksheet>